{0 Middleware composition}

{!Http_kit_middleware.Basic} composes request handlers.
{!Http_kit_middleware.Context} adds an application-selected context type.
{!Http_kit_middleware.Transition} tracks changes to that context across wrappers.

All styles preserve the result type and request body type. They do not choose a
scheduler, body stream, error representation, or response policy. A handler may
return a direct response, an application result, or a native runtime promise.

Composition is outermost first. Short-circuiting and exception behavior remain
visible to the application. Transition composition checks the data passed to endpoints;
they do not establish the semantic truth of an authentication decision.
